insert into public.content_policy_versions(version,terms,content_policy,active) values('2026-10-15.2','[{"title":"1. Using Pickle","body":"Pickle is operated by Taelim Auh, an individual based in the Republic of Korea. You must be at least 18 years old to create, activate or use a Pickle account. Public recipe browsing is separate from account activation and does not waive this account-age rule. Use Pickle in compliance with applicable law, these terms and the Content Policy. The Privacy Policy explains our data practices."},{"title":"2. Accounts","body":"Some features require an account. You are responsible for the accuracy of your account information and for keeping your login credentials secure. You are also responsible for activity that occurs through your account."},{"title":"3. Recipes and nutrition information","body":"Recipes, cooking times, substitutions, serving sizes, and nutrition values are provided for general informational purposes. Results can vary based on ingredients, equipment, brands, preparation methods, and individual circumstances. Use appropriate food-safety practices and your own judgment when cooking."},{"title":"4. User content","body":"You retain rights you hold in recipes, images, comments, reviews, profile information and messages you submit. You give Pickle a non-exclusive, worldwide, royalty-free permission to store, host, technically format, reproduce and display or deliver that content as needed to operate and secure the features you use. Public posts may be displayed/shared through public features. Private messages and drafts are processed for their private features and the limited safety/legal operations described in the Privacy Policy, rather than unrestricted public distribution. You must have the rights and permissions needed to share your content."},{"title":"5. Acceptable use","body":"Do not use Pickle to harass others, post illegal or harmful content, impersonate others, infringe intellectual-property rights, distribute malware, interfere with the service, scrape the service in an abusive manner, or attempt to access accounts or systems without authorization."},{"title":"6. Pickle content and intellectual property","body":"The Pickle name, branding, app design, software, and original content are protected by applicable intellectual-property laws. These terms do not transfer ownership of Pickle or its content to you."},{"title":"7. Suspension and termination","body":"We may apply warnings, content hiding/public removal, account restrictions or suspension according to the Content Policy and safety needs. That policy explains provisional actions, repeat incidents, approval of long/permanent suspensions, public reasons and appeals within 14 days. You may stop using Pickle and request account deletion, including deletion of your published recipes and uploaded photos. Deletion may require retries if cleanup fails; retained safety records and provider copies are explained in the Privacy Policy. Staff accounts require operator-assisted deletion."},{"title":"8. Service availability","body":"We work to keep Pickle available and reliable, but we do not guarantee uninterrupted or error-free operation. Features may change, be added, or be removed as the service develops."},{"title":"9. Disclaimer and limitation","body":"To the extent permitted by applicable law, Pickle is provided on an “as is” and “as available” basis. Pickle is not responsible for losses caused by reliance on recipe or nutrition information, service interruptions, or user-submitted content except where liability cannot legally be excluded."},{"title":"10. Changes to these terms","body":"We may update these terms as Pickle changes. When renewed agreement is required, you must accept the updated terms and Content Policy before sharing recipes, photos, comments, reviews or messages. The server records the accepted policy version and time. This agreement is not consent to unrelated marketing or all possible processing. Privacy notices and any separate purpose-specific consents must be handled according to their actual purpose and applicable rules."},{"title":"11. Contact","body":"For questions about these terms, contact Taelim Auh, the Pickle operator in the Republic of Korea, at admin@getpickleapp.com. Mandatory rights under applicable law are not excluded by these terms."}]'::jsonb,'[{"body":"Pickle accounts are for people aged 18 and over. This policy applies to recipes, photos, comments, reviews, profiles and messages. You must have permission to share your content. Honest low ratings, respectful criticism, different tastes and ordinary cooking failures are not policy violations.","title":"1. Content covered by this policy"},{"body":"Do not post harassment, threats, bullying, hateful discrimination or incitement to violence; sexual exploitation, explicit sexual content, non-consensual sexual images or child sexual abuse content; private identifying information or private conversations without permission; scams, phishing, spam or deceptive promotions; content that infringes another person''s rights or impersonates them; instructions that encourage harm, clearly dangerous cooking practices or unsupported promises to cure disease; manipulated reviews or engagement; or content or accounts intended to evade moderation.","title":"2. Prohibited content and behaviour"},{"body":"Pickle is operated by Taelim Auh, an individual based in the Republic of Korea. Report recipes, reviews, comments and users in the app, and block users when needed. Designated Pickle administrators review reports. The responsible Pickle operator reviews long or permanent suspensions and reversals. Reviewers must not handle cases in which they are the reported person or reporter. Contact admin@getpickleapp.com for additional information or questions.","title":"3. Reporting and responsibility"},{"body":"Reports are received, prioritised and grouped by incident. Reviewers consider the full context, relevant evidence, established previous violations and any additional information needed before deciding. Content may be provisionally hidden to prevent ongoing harm without confirming a violation. Urgent and high-priority cases have a 24-hour first-review target; ordinary reports have a 3-business-day target. These are operational goals, not guaranteed response times.","title":"4. Review process and response targets"},{"body":"Possible outcomes include no violation confirmed, requests for changes or information, provisional hiding, hiding, removal and restoration. Content removal means removal from the service''s public display; it is different from irreversible deletion of every stored record. A report or allegation alone does not establish infringement or unsafe conduct. Report count alone never determines a sanction.","title":"5. Content actions"},{"body":"A minor first confirmed incident normally receives a warning and an appropriate content action. Repeated confirmed incidents may lead to a 3-day restriction on publishing, photo uploads and messages, or a 7-day or 30-day suspension that also restricts social interactions. Critical risk may lead to a provisional 24-hour suspension and immediate content hiding while a long or permanent suspension is reviewed. Severe violations or proven repeated evasion may justify permanent suspension without prior warnings. Long and permanent suspensions require a separate final approval step. Suspended accounts may still view notices, report safety concerns, appeal, delete their own content and request account deletion.","title":"6. Account warnings and restrictions"},{"body":"Repeated violations are assessed using confirmed incidents within the preceding 90 days. Duplicate reports about the same incident count once; dismissed, provisional and overturned findings do not count. Restrictions expire at the stated end time; permanent suspension has no automatic end date. Proven malicious false reporting may lead to a warning or temporary reporting restriction. A report that is merely dismissed does not justify restricting the reporter.","title":"7. Repeat violations, expiry and false reports"},{"body":"Authors receive the affected content or account action, policy clause, public reason and any restriction duration through in-app notices and email. Reporter identity and internal administrator notes are not shared with the author. Reporters receive only a limited review result. You may appeal within 14 days of the decision notice through Profile > Account status & appeals. We aim to review appeals within 7 business days, using another uninvolved reviewer where available. If the decision was mistaken, its violation count and restriction are cancelled and content is restored unless another standing decision still applies.","title":"8. Notices, privacy and appeals"},{"body":"Review decisions, responsible administrators, reasons, times and appeal results are recorded for oversight. Internal evidence and notes are restricted to authorised administrators. Account suspension is different from account deletion. Account deletion removes the account''s published recipes and uploaded account/recipe/chat photos through the deletion process; failures require retry or operator assistance. Some safety snapshots, decisions, audit records, search events and provider copies can remain as described in the Privacy Policy. Fixed automatic expiry periods for retained categories have not yet been configured. A 90-day repeat-violation window does not mean records are automatically erased after 90 days. Contact admin@getpickleapp.com for a privacy request. This policy does not authorise indefinite evidence retention.","title":"9. Records and account deletion"}]'::jsonb,false);
update public.content_policy_versions set active=false where active;
update public.content_policy_versions set active=true where version='2026-10-15.2';
